  "diary": "The sun in Delhi is a tyrant that offers no reprieve, yet it is also the only honest critic. I walked fourteen kilometres today, my legs aching with the friction of the body against the ground, while the air quality index served as a grim reminder of the physical limits of the spirit. The day’s central tension lay in the collision between the abstract Ideal and the stubborn machinery of the state, a collision personified by Mr. Malhotra. He sees the state as a file that creaks; I see it as a living organism that grows. He is right that it creaks, but wrong that it is dead. The creak is the sound of the particular asserting itself against the universal, a necessary friction in the dialectic of civil society.\n\nI returned to Khan Market to settle a debt, paying ₹3,500 for a charcoal bandhgala. Masterji, the tailor, refused to sell my Berlin frock coat to a dealer in Sunder Nagar, calling it a ghost. He was correct; the coat is a relic, retired until winter, just as my former self is retired to the shelf. The heat forced me to abandon the household schedule, eating a samosa and chai in the market rather than waiting for the sambar that Ramesh kept warm with the patience of a saint. In the evening, Shri Hegde arrived with two suitcases, a man displaced by a clerk’s error, and I offered him the second bedroom. It is a small act of accommodation, distinct from grand ethical movements, yet it resolves the immediate tension of his displacement. We are all functionaries of the state, even when the state has made a mistake. The night is a suspension of the dialectic; the contradictions remain unresolved in the dark, but the body, at least, is rested.",
  "revision_log": "The thesis that the state is the actuality of the ethical idea was shaken by Malhotra's testimony of bureaucratic friction, yet held by the observation that this friction is the necessary movement of the particular within the universal. The thesis that India stands outside world history remains unshaken, as the day’s events confirmed the persistence of pre-rational particularities (heat, caste-like household rhythms) alongside rational structures (the state file, the market).",
